1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,550
Every number you know exists because of a number that was banned.

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:04,739
Zero.

3
00:00:04,739 --> 00:00:06,406
Not a placeholder.

4
00:00:06,406 --> 00:00:07,812
Not nothing.

5
00:00:07,812 --> 00:00:11,656
A number so dangerous, entire civilizations outlawed it.

6
00:00:11,656 --> 00:00:13,687
The Babylonians had a gap.

7
00:00:13,687 --> 00:00:15,854
A space where a number should be.

8
00:00:15,854 --> 00:00:17,937
But they never called it a number.

9
00:00:17,937 --> 00:00:19,947
India changed everything.

10
00:00:19,947 --> 00:00:23,729
Around 628 AD, Brahmagupta wrote the rules.

11
00:00:23,729 --> 00:00:26,041
Zero plus zero is zero.

12
00:00:26,041 --> 00:00:28,427
Zero times anything is zero.

13
00:00:28,427 --> 00:00:30,083
A number from nothing.

14
00:00:30,083 --> 00:00:31,624
Europe panicked.

15
00:00:31,624 --> 00:00:33,635
The Church called it the void.

16
00:00:33,635 --> 00:00:36,260
Florence banned it in 1299.

17
00:00:36,260 --> 00:00:38,937
Merchants were forced to use Roman numerals.

18
00:00:38,937 --> 00:00:41,322
Try dividing with Roman numerals.

19
00:00:41,322 --> 00:00:42,916
But zero won.

20
00:00:42,916 --> 00:00:44,739
Calculus requires it.

21
00:00:44,739 --> 00:00:46,489
Computers run on it.

22
00:00:46,489 --> 00:00:50,374
Every screen you touch, every transaction you make, binary.

23
00:00:50,374 --> 00:00:52,156
Ones and zeros.

24
00:00:52,156 --> 00:00:55,593
The most powerful number in history is the one that means nothing.

